{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevSaddleWindow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Knot.KashaevSaddleWindow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.KashaevWindowAssembly"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_sum_kashaevProd_saddle_window_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.abs_sum_kashaevProd_saddle_window_le","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevSaddleWindow.lean#L85-L153","doc":"**The Kashaev window against the Gaussian closed form.**\n\nThe hypotheses are exactly what a caller can check: the window's angular range\nsits inside `(0, π)`, `1/sin²` and `|cot|` are bounded there, and `B` dominates\nstep 10's per-pair bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.angle_mem_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.angle_mem_window","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevSaddleWindow.lean#L63-L83","doc":"Every index in the window has its angle inside the window's angular range.\nMonotonicity of `x ↦ xπ/N`, nothing more — but it is what lets one pair of\nangular hypotheses serve every `k'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevGaussCoeff_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevGaussCoeff_pos","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevSaddleWindow.lean#L43-L61","doc":"`a > 0` exactly when the angle is past `π/2` — which is where the saddle\n`5π/6` lives, and is why the summand is a Gaussian rather than a growing\nexponential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevTilt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevTilt","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevSaddleWindow.lean#L39-L41","doc":"The tilt at index `k`: `L = log(2 sin θ_k)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevGaussCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Knot.FigureEightVolume.kashaevGaussCoeff","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Knot/KashaevSaddleWindow.lean#L35-L37","doc":"The Gaussian coefficient at index `k`: `a = −π·cot θ_k / N`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}